-- title:
--   Principal congruence levels are cofinal in neighbourhoods of 1
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field, with ring of integers $\mathcal{O}_K$, and let $V$ be a subset of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ — the group `AdelicGL2 (𝓞 K) K`, i.e. the general linear group of $2\times 2$ matrices over the adele ring of $K$ — which is a neighbourhood of the identity matrix. Then there is a natural number $m$ such that the subgroup
--   $$\big(\mathrm{principalLevel}\ \text{at the ideal } (m+1)\mathcal{O}_K\big)\ \cap\ \mathrm{finiteAdelicGL2Subgroup}\ K,$$
--   viewed as a subset of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$, is contained in $V$. Here the ideal in question is `Ideal.span {((m + 1 : ℕ) : 𝓞 K)}`, the principal ideal generated by the image of the positive integer $m+1$; `principalLevel` at an ideal $N$ is the intersection of `levelOne` at $N$ — the preimage under the map $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)\to\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_{K,f})$ of the finite-adelic subgroup `finiteLevelOne` at $N$ — with its image under conjugation by the permutation matrix `weyl` $=\bigl(\begin{smallmatrix}0&1\\1&0\end{smallmatrix}\bigr)$; and `finiteAdelicGL2Subgroup K` is the kernel of the homomorphism `glArch`, induced on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ by the projection of $\mathbb{A}_K$ to the infinite adeles, so its elements are exactly those $g$ with trivial archimedean component.
--
--   This is the statement that the principal congruence subgroups $K(m+1)$ of the finite-adelic group, indexed by rational integers, are cofinal among neighbourhoods of the identity in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$; it supplies a countable family of open subgroups over which later arguments may run. It is used in the construction of a common level for smooth automorphic functions ([`AutomorphicForm.exists_ne_bot_forall_apply_mul_eq_of_mem_principalLevel_of_isKfSmooth_of_differentiable`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_ne_bot_forall_apply_mul_eq_of_mem_principalLevel_of_isKfSmooth_of_differentiable)) and in [`AutomorphicForm.paleyWiener_sections_levelTypeAverage_of_kernel_maximalCompact_detOne`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.paleyWiener_sections_levelTypeAverage_of_kernel_maximalCompact_detOne).
